ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi103: Two ADVANCED_FACEs on PLANEs in a CLOSED_SHELL; face0: 4-edge S-curve (figure-eight crossing) wire on a PLANE at z=0; P0=(0,0,0), P1=(10,10,0), P2=(0,10,0), P3=(10,0,0); E0(P0→P1) and E2(P2→P3) are crossing diagonals — self-intersecting pair; E1(P1→P2) and E3(P3→P0) connect the crossing loop; wire closes (P0 start = P0 end via E3) but topology is a figure-eight; ShapeFix_Wire.FixSelfIntersectingEdge hits 30-iteration hard limit and exits silently without reporting convergence failure — IS the mechanism; face1 is a correct 10x10 square at z=-1; all EDGE_CURVEs ARE wired into EDGE_LOOPs → FACE_OUTER_BOUNDs → ADVANCED_FACEs in CLOSED_SHELL — never orphaned */
